  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-gibbiceps-2/",
      "html": "<p>The red highfin sucker is a classic, which found its lovers long before the invention of the L-numbers. Juveniles are really adorable and excellent algae killers. In addition they look very beautiful. Since this catfish easily grows to 30-40 cm in length, there are two camps among aquarists. Some are critical of the animal because of its achievable final size (\"everyone must have fallen for it\"), others use the opportunity to finally acquire the long desired large tank.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-gibbiceps-2/",
      "html": "<p>The Glyptoperichthys gibbiceps in the trade are meanwhile almost without exception offspring from Southeast Asia.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-gibbiceps-2/",
      "html": "<p>The wild species is very widespread in South America (the entire upper and middle basins of the Amazon and Orinoco: Bolivia, Brazil, Ecuador, Peru, Colombia and Venezuela), but is hardly ever imported from there.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/glyptoperichthys-gibbiceps-2/",
      "html": "<p>The care of the peaceful animals is completely problem-free, if one does justice to their space requirements.</p>"
    }
  ],
